{
  "name": "sauropod_gate",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "saurischia",
  "notes": "The triumphal city gate: a limestone block 18 m wide and 6 m deep, 19 m to the parapet, with one great arch 9 m wide and 13 m to its crown, and a 3 m pedestrian arch each side, pilasters, a cornice and an attic. Its axis runs along local Z (walk through it front to back); it carves the three passages.",
